---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="AI Assessment: Two to four weeks, fixed price, you own the output"
  description="Before you build anything, find out where the numbers actually come from, what the current setup costs, and what to fix first. A paid assessment for owner-led firms, distributors, and organizations with an AI mandate and no plan."
>
  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="pill">The assessment</span>
        <h1 class="hero-title">Find out what's actually broken before you pay anyone to fix it.</h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">Two to four weeks at a fixed price. We map where your numbers come from, what the current setup costs you, and what to fix first. You own everything we produce, whether or not you ever work with us again.</p>
        <div class="hero-buttons">
          <a href="https://links.zenprocess.ai/widget/booking/rcoKJifJJA46bRI9fTEr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
          <a href="/resources/what-a-paid-ai-audit-looks-like" class="btn btn-ghost">Read what's in it</a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-eyebrow">Led by Vinh Truong, CISSP. 20+ yrs VP/CTO · $80M+ initiatives.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="brief">
        <div class="bar"><b>Assessment report</b><span style="opacity:.8">Sample</span><span class="r">Week 3 of 3</span></div>
        <div class="body">
          <div class="health" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)">
            <div class="h"><div class="lbl-s">Reports and handoffs mapped</div><div class="n">40</div></div>
            <div class="h"><div class="lbl-s">Manual, by hand</div><div class="n" style="color:#b45309">28</div></div>
            <div class="h"><div class="lbl-s">Producing conflicting numbers</div><div class="n" style="color:#dc3545">7</div></div>
            <div class="h" style="background:var(--green-tint);border-color:var(--green-tint-2)"><div class="lbl-s">Recommendations, ranked</div><div class="n" style="color:var(--green-d)">5</div></div>
          </div>
          <p class="lbl-s" style="margin-top:14px">Fix first</p>
          <div class="sample-list">
            <div class="sample-row"><span class="sample-dot" style="background:#dc3545"></span><div><b>Daily out-of-stock check</b><div class="eyebrow">2 hrs/day by hand · automate first</div></div></div>
            <div class="sample-row"><span class="sample-dot" style="background:#f59e0b"></span><div><b>Three versions of "the numbers"</b><div class="eyebrow">purchasing, finance, sales · one source</div></div></div>
            <div class="sample-row"><span class="sample-dot" style="background:var(--green)"></span><div><b>ERP reporting is fine as-is</b><div class="eyebrow">train the team · no build needed</div></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-familiar reveal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="section-title">Three kinds of company book this</h2>
      <div class="familiar-grid">
        <div class="card familiar-card"><h3 class="familiar-title">A distributor whose ERP data nobody trusts</h3><p class="familiar-desc">SAP or NetSuite runs the transactions. Purchasing runs the day out of Excel. Three teams keep three spreadsheets and none of them agree.</p></div>
        <div class="card familiar-card"><h3 class="familiar-title">An owner-led firm running across too many tools</h3><p class="familiar-desc">The books, the CRM, the inbox, and the calendar each hold part of the picture. Every morning you reassemble it by hand, and things slip in the gaps.</p></div>
        <div class="card familiar-card"><h3 class="familiar-title">An organization told to "do something with AI"</h3><p class="familiar-desc">There's a mandate and a budget, and no map of which processes are ready, which data can be trusted, or what the first project should be.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-build reveal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="section-title">What you get</h2>
      <p class="build-subtitle">A working document your team can use regardless of what you do next, instead of a slide deck built to scare you into a contract.</p>
      <div class="build-grid">
        <div class="card build-card"><p class="lbl-s build-label">Map</p><h3 class="build-title">Where every number comes from</h3><p class="build-desc">Every system and every spreadsheet, including the reports someone builds by hand each week. Most companies have never seen this laid out.</p></div>
        <div class="card build-card"><p class="lbl-s build-label">Cost</p><h3 class="build-title">What today costs you</h3><p class="build-desc">The hours spent assembling numbers, the decisions delayed because nobody trusts them, and the errors that reached a customer, added up with the math shown.</p></div>
        <div class="card build-card"><p class="lbl-s build-label">Gaps</p><h3 class="build-title">Where it breaks</h3><p class="build-desc">The places where the same question gets three answers, or a decision gets made without data that already exists. Ranked by what each one costs.</p></div>
        <div class="card build-card build-card-featured"><p class="lbl-s build-label">Plan</p><h3 class="build-title">What to fix first</h3><p class="build-desc">Specific recommendations in order, each with an estimated cost, timeline, and return. Not tied to any vendor, so any team can build from it.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-engagements reveal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="section-title">How it runs</h2>
      <div class="eng-grid">
        <div class="card eng-card"><div class="mono eng-num">01</div><h3 class="eng-title">Follow the numbers</h3><p class="eng-desc">We sit with the people who do the work, not just the org chart. We trace a purchase order, a sales order, an invoice, from creation to wherever the number ends up.</p></div>
        <div class="card eng-card"><div class="mono eng-num">02</div><h3 class="eng-title">Put a cost on it</h3><p class="eng-desc">Every manual step gets an hourly cost and every mismatch gets a risk. We pull real transactions rather than estimates, so the number holds up in front of a CFO.</p></div>
        <div class="card eng-card"><div class="mono eng-num">03</div><h3 class="eng-title">Hand you the plan</h3><p class="eng-desc">Ranked by return rather than by what's easiest to sell. If the honest answer is "your setup is fine, train the team," that's the answer you get.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-after reveal">
    <div class="wrap after-wrap">
      <h2 class="section-title">What happens after</h2>
      <div class="after-grid">
        <div class="card after-card">
          <h3 class="after-title">You build with us</h3>
          <p class="after-desc">Phase 1 is the highest-return item from the report, scoped and priced from what the assessment found. Four to eight weeks, and you see real output before there's a Phase 2. For a distributor that's usually <a href="/for-distributors">ERP Intelligence</a>, for an owner-led firm it's usually <a href="/owner-os">OwnerOS</a>, and for an organization with an AI mandate it's the first project on the map.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card after-card">
          <h3 class="after-title">You build with someone else, or nobody</h3>
          <p class="after-desc">The report is yours, and the plan isn't tied to any vendor, on purpose. Take it to another firm, hand it to your own team, or put it on a shelf and come back in six months. The analysis still holds.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="after-note">The assessment is priced on its own and paid when it's delivered. That's deliberate. We aren't funded by the project it might lead to, so there's no reason for us to inflate what we find.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-proof reveal text-center">
    <div class="wrap proof-wrap">
      <span class="kicker">What one assessment led to, for a national building materials distributor</span>
      <div class="stats proof-stats">
        <div><div class="n">3,000+</div><div class="eyebrow">SKUs, multi-warehouse SAP</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">800+</div><div class="eyebrow">daily exceptions flagged</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">0%</div><div class="eyebrow">variance versus SAP</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">16 wks</div><div class="eyebrow">assessment to daily use</div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="proof-note"><a href="/case-study">Read the case study</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-final-cta reveal text-center">
    <div class="wrap final-cta-wrap">
      <h2 class="final-cta-title">Tell me what is slipping. I will tell you if we can help.</h2>
      <p class="final-cta-desc">A 30-minute call. We look at how you run today and whether an assessment would find enough to justify what it costs. If it wouldn't, I'd rather say so on the call.</p>
      <a href="https://links.zenprocess.ai/widget/booking/rcoKJifJJA46bRI9fTEr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary btn-large">Book a call</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero-section {
    background: var(--hero-glow);
    padding-top: 84px;
    padding-bottom: 64px;
  }
  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.05fr .95fr;
    gap: 56px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .hero-title {
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.6vw, 54px);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin: 20px 0 18px;
  }
  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .hero-buttons {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .hero-eyebrow {
    margin-top: 22px;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .sample-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .sample-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .sample-dot {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    flex: none;
    margin-top: 5px;
  }
  .section-familiar {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .section-title {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.6vw, 40px);
    font-weight: 800;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 44px;
  }
  .familiar-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .familiar-card {
    padding: 28px;
  }
  .familiar-title {
    font-size: 19px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .familiar-desc {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .section-build {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--canvas-2);
  }
  .build-subtitle {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 0 auto 44px;
  }
  .build-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .build-card {
    padding: 24px;
  }
  .build-card-featured {
    border-color: var(--green-tint-2);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--green-tint), transparent 40%), var(--card);
  }
  .build-label {
    color: var(--green-d);
  }
  .build-title {
    font-size: 18px;
    margin: 8px 0;
  }
  .build-desc {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 14.5px;
  }
  .section-engagements {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .eng-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .eng-card {
    padding: 28px;
  }
  .eng-num {
    font-size: 40px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--green-d);
  }
  .eng-title {
    font-size: 20px;
    margin: 14px 0 8px;
  }
  .eng-desc {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .section-after {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--canvas-2);
  }
  .after-wrap {
    max-width: 960px;
  }
  .after-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .after-card {
    padding: 28px;
  }
  .after-title {
    font-size: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .after-desc {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .after-desc a {
    color: var(--green-d);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .after-note {
    margin: 32px auto 0;
    max-width: 720px;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .section-proof {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .proof-wrap {
    max-width: 900px;
  }
  .proof-stats {
    margin-top: 26px;
  }
  .proof-note {
    margin-top: 30px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .proof-note a {
    color: var(--green-d);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .section-final-cta {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--hero-glow);
  }
  .final-cta-wrap {
    max-width: 680px;
  }
  .final-cta-title {
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 46px);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .final-cta-desc {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .btn-large {
    font-size: 16px;
    padding: 16px 28px;
  }
  @media(max-width:860px) {
    .hero-grid, .familiar-grid, .build-grid, .eng-grid, .after-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
      gap: 32px;
    }
    .stats {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      gap: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
